---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '2026-10-24';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Security"
  description="How PromptDNS handles security: client-side lookups with no backend database, TLS via Cloudflare, and responsible disclosure at security@promptdns.com."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Security</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Security at PromptDNS</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-ink-faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        PromptDNS today is a static website on Cloudflare Pages. Every tool runs in your browser,
        queries public DNS resolvers directly, and sends nothing to a PromptDNS server - because
        there is no PromptDNS server in the lookup path. There are no user accounts and no
        database of your lookups.
      </p>

      <h2>What this means in practice</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Domain lookups never reach us.</strong> Your browser sends DoH queries to public resolvers (Cloudflare, Google, AliDNS). We cannot log, store, or sell what you look up, because it never passes through anything we operate.</li>
        <li><strong>No accounts, no passwords</strong> - nothing to breach today. The only database is the early-access list: your email, an optional domain, the referring tool, and a hashed IP for flood limiting.</li>
        <li><strong>Transport security</strong> is provided by Cloudflare TLS on every page. HSTS and a full security-header set are being rolled out; see our own tool results improve as we apply them.</li>
        <li><strong>Email you send us</strong> (support, bugs, security) is handled by our email provider and read only by us.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>When accounts arrive</h2>
      <p>
        Monitoring accounts are in development. Before launch, credentials will be stored hashed,
        authentication endpoints rate-limited, and sessions protected against CSRF - we will
        update this page as those systems ship, and we will say exactly what data the monitoring
        service stores (the DNS records of domains you add, and the alerts they generate).
      </p>

      <h2>Responsible disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Found a vulnerability? Email
        <a href="mailto:security@promptdns.com" class="text-accent">security@promptdns.com</a>.
        We acknowledge within 72 hours and will work with you on coordinated disclosure. Please
        give us time to fix before publishing, and avoid automated scanning that could degrade
        service for others.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
